# Component size limit (400 lines)

React components and other `.tsx` modules in this repo must stay **at or under 400 lines** (including imports, types, and exports).

## When adding or editing TSX

- Before growing a file past ~350 lines, extract subcomponents, hooks, or pure helpers into colocated files.
- Prefer `ComponentName/` folders with `index.tsx`, `SubPart.tsx`, and `useComponentName.ts` over one monolithic file.
- Spec/data-heavy TSX (e.g. canvas specs) should split layout from data constants or move static config to `.ts` files.

## How to split

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — 800-line CanvasShell.tsx with camera, graph, and toolbar inline

// ✅ GOOD — CanvasShell.tsx orchestrates; hooks and presentational pieces live beside it
// CanvasShell.tsx (~200 lines)
// useCanvasCamera.ts
// CanvasToolbar.tsx
```

## Check violations locally

From the repo root:

```bash
find . \( -path ./node_modules -o -path ./.next \) -prune -o -name '*.tsx' -print |
  while read -r f; do
    n=$(wc -l < "$f" | tr -d ' ')
    [ "$n" -gt 400 ] && printf '%s %s\n' "$n" "$f"
  done | sort -rn
```

Treat any file over 400 lines as tech debt: refactor when touching that area, or split as part of the current task if the change would push the file further over the limit.
